Shopify’s Storefront API does not expose `on_hand` or `reserved` inventory quantities; it exposes `quantityAvailable` on `StoreAvailability`, which is physically on-hand stock only and excludes transferable stock. [1] For SKU-level `on_hand` and `reserved`, use the Admin GraphQL `inventoryLevel` query with `quantities(names: ["on_hand","reserved"])`; it also returns the associated SKU. [2]

query { inventoryLevel(id: "...") { quantities(names: ["on_hand","reserved"]) { name quantity } item { sku } } }

